Z||000008||Tweek||05-21-2001||09:15 AM||||Hey, I friend of mine just last week picked up an 87 Conquest Tsi, Its quite a zippy little car! Was wondering though, where do you go to find parts for it (conquest/starion)?, there are a few things that he is having quite a hard time finding, such as a new gas tank. though I think hes just gonna have it reconditioned at this point.  See ya||||reg||1
Z||000009||BV MotorSports||05-21-2001||05:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Welcome, I am currently doing a Caddy 4.5 swap, ever do one of these?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not personally but there is a shop in Stuarts Draft VA (on or near that city just off I64/I81) that has done many. They also have one with a 500ci caddy w/ nos in a Tesstarossa kit. I was there when the wheelie bars came in for it. If memory serves me correct the shop is called Nesbit & Associates. They did some work on a '66 Corvair Monza I owned. I will look and see if I can find their contact info.<BR>Good luck on your kit.<P>BTW what trans are you going to use? The Olds v8 FWD trans?<P>Steven||||reg||1
Z||000010||BV MotorSports||05-21-2001||05:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tweek:<BR><B>Hey, I friend of mine just last week picked up an 87 Conquest Tsi, Its quite a zippy little car! Was wondering though, where do you go to find parts for it (conquest/starion)?, there are a few things that he is having quite a hard time finding, such as a new gas tank. though I think hes just gonna have it reconditioned at this point.  See ya</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nice to hear that another StarQuest has been saved from the j-yard or rusting in someones yard! They are pretty neat cars. Kinda like fieros, buy one then the next thing ya know they start to multiply!<BR>There are tons of mods/tricks for those cars. Feel free to contact me or check out my web page: <A HREF="http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1" TARGET=_blank>http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1</A>  and look for the Conquest link. I have alot of info about "free mods", "how too" and links to sites and shops dedicated to them. Its way more usefull than the fiero info on my page but....thats about to change.<P><BR>Steven<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||05-22-2001||08:05 AM||||Welcome to the forum.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000012||Songman||05-22-2001||08:42 AM||||Beautiful Fiero you got there... and I have always liked those Conquests. Looked at a few over the years but they are kinda like Trans Ams, Camaros, etc.. Usually ragged out or people think they are worth about double what they really are.. I'll find me one someday... I like white (or black) with dark tinted windows...<P>Welcome to the Forum!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
Z||000013||rodmcneill||05-22-2001||09:39 AM||||Welcome, nice website!||||reg||14
Z||000014||BV MotorSports||05-22-2001||10:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Beautiful Fiero you got there... and I have always liked those Conquests. Looked at a few over the years but they are kinda like Trans Ams, Camaros, etc.. Usually ragged out or people think they are worth about double what they really are.. I'll find me one someday... I like white (or black) with dark tinted windows...<P>Welcome to the Forum!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Funny thing is, the Conquest was a 22k car back in 87. The fiero was 14k (or so). Guess which one rides better, is quieter, tighter and prettier? Thats right, the Fiero! iTS NIGHT AND DAY BETWEEN THE 2. I am amazed at how tight the fiero has remained over the yrs. Now the 'Quest is far faster and *gulp* handles better but thats about it for my "Jap mustang".<BR>Ah someday I will have it as nice as the Fiero.<P>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||05-22-2001||04:24 PM||||I liked the conquest too. loved the bulging fenders like a muscled Porsch 944. Werent they a Mopar ??||||reg||1
Z||000016||BV MotorSports||05-22-2001||05:08 PM||||Yeah thats what attracted me to the StarQuest<BR>(conquest/starion) was the "wide body". Looks mean. Yeah....I get the "hey thats a nice 944 you got"! Heheheheh not bad company to be in.<BR>Better than my fiero being called a <BR>"ferrar-E-OH".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Heck what other car has ABS, Auto-climate control, 4 wheel independant suspension, RWD, 3.54 Limited slip rear diff, Leather, cruise, all the bells and whistles, Turbo charged/intercooled, 16 inch wheels and a factory alarm that you can pick up all day long for less than 2.5k? (my 85.5 ESi is one of 200 made and I got it for FREE!!) They have like ZERO resale value and I love it.....I can keep getting them cheap! <BR>Going to the track this weekend to see what she runs, I thinking low 14's high 13's.<P>Check out my web page if ya want to learn more as well as check out the turbo & hi tech article on them. <P>BTW.... Chrysler Conquest, Mitsubishi Starion<BR>Are sister cars like the Camaro/Firebird but with way less distinction between the 2. Little more than badges and tail lights.<P><A HREF="http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1" TARGET=_blank>http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1</A> <P>Steven<P><BR>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi<p>[This message has been edited by BV MotorSports (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jay||05-22-2001||06:39 PM||||Hey, BV cool site.  That photo of the 454 in the front of the Fiero, where did you get that from?  Reason I ask is because I took that photo about 4 years ago at the Toronto clubs first annual show.  Have we met?  If you want, I got tons of pictures from various shows and you can also link to my web page in my signature, I'll do the same for you when I update my page.  BTW that 454 Fiero is now Viper blue.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
