Z||000020||BV MotorSports||05-22-2001||09:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Hey, BV cool site.  That photo of the 454 in the front of the Fiero, where did you get that from?  Reason I ask is because I took that photo about 4 years ago at the Toronto clubs first annual show.  Have we met?  If you want, I got tons of pictures from various shows and you can also link to my web page in my signature, I'll do the same for you when I update my page.  BTW that 454 Fiero is now Viper blue.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To be honest I cant remember where I found that photo... I thought it was really cool and loaded it onto my page. I'll be checking out your site later. Feel free to use anything on my site, as long as you dont claim it as your own. (has happened b4!)<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000021||BV MotorSports||05-22-2001||10:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>Welcome ! I checked out your site and saw some pics of the turbo duke. Did you own that car? Just wondering you you had any info on it. Like performance numbers, and what turbo it had. Also did the engine hold up with it?<P>Thanks   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, I bought that turbo'ed 84 from a local guy. He didnt have a clue about it and was driving around w/ a huge exhaust leak that prevented it from making any boost.<BR>The turbo kit was sold by IRM (Jim Sutter) and just about everything else on it came from IRM as well.<BR>I bought that car for $800 bucks and started fixing it up and removing the "ghetto" look.<BR>Ordered some parts from Jim and had the turbo all fixed and took her to the car wash to clean the engine bay and underneath the car. As I pulled into the car wash I saw black smoke coming from the engine bay vents. Yep....ENGINE FIRE!!!! Seems that brand new braided oil line grounded out on a melted wire I hadnt noticed (remember this guy was driving it with a huge exhaust leak).<BR>I got her home by capping the feed line and making sure the turbo didnt go into boost for the 1/2 mile ride home. Most of the C500 block was melted and I didnt like the turbo being so close to it. I spoke to Ed Parks about updating to the 85-up style wiring harness. And he said its alot of work but he could do it.<BR>Now the car sets at Ed's shop getting fixed up. I should have never sold it but lack of money will make you do strange things. I know it couldnt be in better hands. Plus Ed claims that when he passes on....I'll get her back. I have offered 2 x what he paid for it and he still wont sell her back to me!<BR>Blames it on Rosie but I know Ed knows he has a SUPER RARE car (1 of 10) and he said he plans on being the oldest living human so I guess I have a pretty long wait to get her back.<BR>Turbo is a Mitsubishi turbo that was originally developed for GM while testing a twin turbo vette. Every turbo they found was exactly opposite of what they needed so they had mitsu make this turbo backwards. It even has CHEVROLET cast BACKWARDS on it!!!!!!!!!<BR>At the time I really didnt understand turbos but if I had it now....WOW it would be a monster! As it was it was pretty much even in performance with a v6 fiero.<BR>Hey ED....dont ya want to trade me even for my 87GT? PAAAALEEEEEESSSSSEEEEEE!!!!!!?<BR>Rosie anit gots ta know!<BR>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000022||BV MotorSports||05-25-2001||01:40 AM||||I added a link on my web page to make it easier to find the 84 t-top turbocharged fiero and added pics of my newest addition....SCCA prepped 87 Conquest TSi.<BR>This thing is awsome! Talk about handling like its on rails! WOW! <A HREF="http://home.talkcity/speedwaydr/vinc1/mycar2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.talkcity/speedwaydr/vinc1/mycar2.html</A> <P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000023||danny boy||05-25-2001||11:18 PM||||heh,know anything about twin turbo stealths? Like why after I put the 13G's on boost spikes @ 14psi, then drops to around 7psi? This is w/o boost controller. Or anyone wanting to buy my stock 9b's?<P>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||BV MotorSports||05-26-2001||03:04 PM||||I know that boost spikes are a bad thing! How do you have the wastegate set up?<BR>You may need to "trick" it by using a grainger valve. I use this on my StarQuests and its amazing! I used to have little boost below 4k in 1st but now it spools RIGHT NOW!<BR>You can pick up a grainger valve for less than $40.<BR>Contact me off-list if you need help locating one.<BR>Hmmm with the turbos you are running they are approx 365cfm each......nice!<P>Steven||||reg||1
